   "id": "avodah_zarah.21a.8",
   "daf": "21a",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "בְּחוּצָה לָאָרֶץ וְכוּ׳. שָׂדֶה דְּאִית בֵּיהּ תַּרְתֵּי — גְּזַרוּ בְּהוּ רַבָּנַן, בָּתִּים דְּלֵית בְּהוּ תַּרְתֵּי — לָא גְּזַרוּ בְּהוּ רַבָּנַן.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches that according to Rabbi Meir, «outside of Eretz» Yisrael one may sell houses and rent fields, but one may not sell fields to gentiles. The Gemara explains: «Concerning a field, which has two» problems when it is in Eretz Yisrael, «the Sages issued a decree» preventing its sale even outside of Eretz Yisrael. «Concerning houses, which do not have two» problems, «the Sages did not issue a decree» prohibiting their sale."
  }
